[4302]="7000794D\n1\tDefeat diseased Bristlehides (total: 6)\tDiseased boars roam the lands to the south and east of Archet's gate. Constable Thistlewool thinks that the best way to end the disease afflicting the local boars is to slay those already infected.\n2\tTalk to Constable Thistlewool\tConstable Thistlewool can be found near the ruins of The Mad Badger Inn in Archet. Constable Thistlewool will wish to hear of your success.\n",
[4303]="70067F91\n1\tKhûtra Elder Ilaya has asked for your help in healing some of the afflicted wild goats surrounding Khûtra. The goats can be found in the hills north of Khûtra.\t\n2\tReturn to Elder Ilaya in Khûtra\tReturn to Elder Ilaya in Khûtra.\n",
[4304]="7002BF96\n1\tDefeat shades (total: 3)\tShades can be found at Atburg, south-east of Aculf's camp in the Rushgore. Bagmund has asked you to banish the shades from Atburg and the Rushgore.\n2\tTalk to Eowils outside Atburg in the Rushgore\tEowils is outside Atburg in the Rushgore, south-east of Aculf's camp. Bagmund asked you to report your successes to the scout Eowils.\n",
[4305]="7005AB05\n1\tBurn dwarf bodies (total: 5)\tYou have found dwarf bodies are being used in Angmarim rituals to make wights. You should burn dwarf bodies in Mullach Cagar.\n2\tTalk to Molkha in the valley\tYou have prevented many fallen dwarves from being made into wights. You should return to Molkha in the valley.\n",
[4306]="7002F917\n1\tDefeat White Hand scavengers at the Norcrofts farms (total: 6)\030Defeat White Hand defilers (total: 6)\tThe farmsteads lie at the western edge of the Norcrofts. Cyneswith has asked you to defeat many of the scavengers and defilers that have invaded and dislodged the farmers from their homes.\n2\tReturn to Cyneswith\tCyneswith lies to the east, behind the large Springview Estate. You have removed many of the Orcs from the homes and farmsteads to the west. This act should restore some hope in Cyneswith.\n",
[4307]="70058FEE\n1\tTortured Angmarim can be found in Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr. Múta has asked you to question the Angmarim that have been tortured by the Dourhands and their kin.\t\n2\tTalk to Múta\tMúta can be found in Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr. You have learned what you could from the tortured Angmarim. You should report back to Múta.\n",
[4308]="7006616E\n1\tCollect wood from wood piles (total: 5)\030Collect cloth from banners (total: 5)\tBruidis has asked you to collect wood and cloth from wood piles and banners in Makham Mijann. Makham Mijann lies north of Tadrent.\n2\tTalk to Bruidis in Tadrent\tYou have collected a suitable amount of wood and cloth. You should give these materials to Bruidis in Tadrent.\n",
[4309]="70044307\n1\tDefeat Mordor siege-builders (total: 5)\030Destroy lumber piles (total: 8)\tParth Gladló is located in southern Talath Anor. You should defeat Mordor siege-builders and destroy lumber piles at Parth Gladló.\n2\tSpeak with Tolwin\tSpeak with Tolwin.\n",
[4310]="70020F01\n1\tCollect deserters' orders (total: 5)\tDunlending officers can be found in Lhe Lhechu, south-west of Echad Dagoras. You should collect papers from the Dunlending officers in Fordirith and learn more of the reason for their presence on the borders of the old North Kingdom.\n2\tBring the Dunlending orders to Dagoras\tDagoras is at Echad Dagoras, north-east of Lhe Lhechu. You should return the orders you have found to Dagoras.\n",
[4311]="700493F3\n1\tReturn to the spot where Aiglos lies\tAiglos can be found in Dor Amarth. You should travel back to Aiglos to assess the situation.\n2\tDefeat the Order of the Eye devoted (total: 6)\tThose devoted to the Order of the Eye can be found around Aiglos. You should defeat them to stand any chance of retrieving the spear.\n3\tConfront a devoted\tA wounded devoted can be found near Aiglos. You should confront the wounded devoted from the Order of the Eye.\n4\tConfront the wounded devoted\tA wounded devoted can be found near Aiglos. You should confront the wounded devoted from the Order of the Eye.\n5\tDefeat the Order of the Eye devoted (total: 4)\tThose devoted to the Order of the Eye can be found around Aiglos. You should defeat them if you stand any chance of retrieving the spear.\n6\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas can be found near Aiglos in Dor Amarth. You should speak with Legolas.\n",
[4312]="700262D4\n1\tSample dire beers before the time runs out (total: 6)\tDire beers can be found throughout the Hedge Maze, waiting to be drunk. You should sample dire beers...but beware! They will disorient you on your venture. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tSpeak with Birdie Thornthicket\tBirdie Thornthicket can be found outside the Hedge Maze. You should speak with Birdie Thornthicket and tell her of your success in sampling the dire beers of the maze.\n",
[4313]="7001BE11\n1\tDefeat snow-troll rippers (total: 12)\tSnow-trolls can be found deep within Sarnúr, south of Thorin's Hall, reached through the ruins of Orodost. Snár has asked you to defeat the snow-trolls which dwell in the ancient dwarf-ruins.\n2\tTalk to Snár in Thorin's Hall\tSnár is in Thorin's Hall, north of Orodost, just outside the Blue Stone Garrison. You should return to Snár with news of your success against the snow-trolls.\n",
[4314]="70037081\n1\tDefeat goblin-skirmishers near Oserley\tYou should defeat the goblin-skirmishers who scout the plains near Oserley.\n2\tDefeat goblin-skirmishers near Oserley (total: 8)\tGoblin-skirmishers can be found in the fields west of Oserley. You should defeat the goblin-skirmishers harassing Oserley.\n",
[4315]="7003EA79\n1\tDefeat bats in the South Trollshaws (total: 6)\tThere are bats in the South Trollshaws. While in the South Trollshaws, you should put an end to the spying of the Enemy's bats in the Trollshaws.\n",
[4316]="7004E83F\n1\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain. You encountered a messenger of Erebor who urged you to speak to the King under the Mountain at once.\n2\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have arrived at Erebor and found a number of dwarves pacing restlessly before the King under the Mountain. You should speak to King Thorin III at once.\n3\tListen to King Thorin III speak of Karazgar\030Listen to King Thorin III speak of Vethúg Wintermind\tKing Thorin III has asked you to listen to him speak on matters concerning Karazgar and Vethúg Wintermind.\n4\tListen to King Thorin III speak of Nori\tKing Thorin III has asked you to listen to him speak on matters concerning Nori, the Keeper of the Coffers.\n5\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have learned of the matters troubling King Thorin III and should now heed the will of the King under the Mountain.\n6\tRestless dwarves can be found before the throne of the King under the Mountain. King Thorin III Stonehelm has grown weary of rising tensions among the Dwarves of Erebor, and has asked you to listen to the grievances of his people that he might better understand them.\t\n7\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have heard the grievances of the dwarves of Erebor, and you should now return to King Thorin III.\n8\tDeliver Nori's missive to Dori in the Hall Under the Mountain\tDori can be found in the Hall under the Mountain. King Thorin III has asked you to deliver the missive Nori left behind before he departed Erebor to Dori in the Hall under the Mountain.\n",
[4317]="7004327B\n1\tTalk to Baranor in Arnach\tBaranor can be found in Arnach, which can be reached by travelling east across the Erui at the Crossings or by use of the bridge near the beacon Minlos. Lady Terenis has asked you to travel east to Arnach and aid the guards there in keeping the people of Lossarnach from harm.\n",
[4318]="70066B49\n1\tDiscover Bel Tâkhmar\tDestroying their weapons barrels at Bel Tâkhmar may prevent them from causing further trouble.\n2\tDestroy weapons barrels at Bel Tâkhmar (total: 6)\tDestroying their weapons barrels at Bel Tâkhmar may prevent them from causing further trouble.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many weapons barrels at Bel Tâkhmar.\n",
[4319]="70072EC4\n1\tSpeak to Sorkamâl the Forbearing\tSorkamâl the Forbearing has discovered a way to free their minds and get them out. Use her scroll to free their minds and collect needed supplies for Mizâdi's war effort. Speak to Sorkamâl to be given the scroll.\n2\tUse Free Mind on enthralled servants (total: 5)\030Gather supplies (total: 8)\tSeek out enthralled servants. Free them from control and gather additional supplies throughout the area for the war effort.\n3\tDefeat the Elder Orc reinforcements near the entrance\tSeek out and defeat the Elder Orcs near the entrance.\n4\tDefeat Daithúch Wound-drinker and his minions\tDefeat Daithúch Wound-drinker and his minions to escape.\n",
[4320]="70040B0C\n1\tFight the Corsair overseer\030Reclaim crates (total: 8)\tThe Corsairs can be found along the River Ringló, north-west of Tadrent. Find and defeat the overseer of the Corsair shipping operation. Steal back crates for the merchants of Tadrent.\n2\tSpeak with Bruidis\tBruidis is in the town of Tadrent. You should speak with Bruidis and inform her that you successfully stopped the Corsair shipping operation.\n",
})
